    "scope": "native_products hook counters and MIR scope timers describe the first hooked attempt only; after fresh_context_fallbacks, subsequent ordinary native work has unavailable per-pass counts. Reuse in a discarded attempt is not work avoided by final compilation. Native receipt phase/total times and request wall include the full native fallback; request wall also includes all driver retries. MIR timers are scopes, not a partition of native total. In typed-body sources, mir_parse_ns includes tiny-header parsing, current typed MI/MBB/use-chain construction and parser/header destruction; it is not pure YAML parsing. mir_restore_validate_ns includes target/number/block state, typed recapture equality, domain, MachineVerifier and full MIR equality. Compare timer definitions at each pinned compiler source. Observer v3 IR scopes: key is supported-entry eligibility/current facts/Input/World/pipeline; unpack is complete selected-slot decode; replay includes parse/clone/current validation/AM/cleanup; parse is only MemoryBuffer+parseBitcodeFile construction, excluding later Module destruction, and is already INCLUDED in replay. Capture is the complete afterStage callback, including cheap early-return gates and new-stage packing. Pack is new-stage admission/frame/SHA/zstd/typed metadata/publication and is already INCLUDED in capture. Do not add child timers to parents, call these a partition, or classify original unknown FPM passes as measured overhead. Observer v1/v2 IR scopes are unavailable (None), not zero. Clock overhead stays in request wall. Optional machine_emission V1 describes only the first hooked attempt. captured_functions and captured_capacity_bytes count sealed pending products, not published products; captured_blocks can include partial captures later declined. declined_functions counts the shim domain only, not all SDK eligibility gates. machine_instructions_skipped is logical MI-loop work, mc_replay_events counts actual emitInstruction inputs, and current_cfi_events counts original MI-overload invocations (which may emit no directive). Current MF restore, MachineVerifier, AsmPrinter envelopes, encoder, layout and relaxation still execute. Timers are nested scopes, not additive components of emit_ns; emit_ns is the whole TargetMachineEmitToMemoryBuffer call plus buffer copy, not pure AsmPrinter. Capacity is a receipt sum, not peak RSS. Missing/null/unavailable MC observations remain unknown. A discarded replay is not final work avoided.",
